# Explicit naming (no abbreviations)

Always name identifiers by the full identity they refer to. Never shorten entity/field names in method names, parameters, locals, or DI bindings.

## Rules

- Include the full property identity in the name: `chatId`, `recipientProfileUserId`, `appointmentId` — not `chat`, `recipient`, `appointment`.
- Repository lookup/delete methods must list every key they use:
  - ❌ `findByChatAndRecipient`, `deleteByChatAndRecipient`, `deleteById` (ambiguous)
  - ✅ `findByChatIdAndRecipientProfileUserId`, `deleteByChatIdAndRecipientProfileUserId`, `deleteByAppointmentChatUnreadReminderId`
- Injected dependencies use the full domain name:
  - ❌ `unreadReminderRepository`, `messageRepo`, `chatRepo`
  - ✅ `appointmentChatUnreadReminderRepository`, `appointmentChatMessageRepository`, `appointmentChatRepository`
- Types follow the same rule: `IStaleUnreadAppointmentChatPair`, not `IStaleUnreadChatPair`.
- Abbreviations like `repo`, `msg`, `usr`, `res`, `req`, `cfg`, `ctx` (as name stems) are forbidden for new code. Prefer the full word.

## Why

Ambiguous names hide which id/field is meant (`recipient` vs `recipientProfileUserId`). Explicit names make call sites self-documenting and prevent wrong-argument bugs.
